📝 QUESTION:
Write a Java program that takes an integer N (size of array), then fills an array of size N with values (you may assume values are sequential like 1,2,3,...). 
After that, take a target sum from the user and determine whether any continuous subarray adds up exactly to this target. 
Use the sliding window technique, where you expand the window by moving the right pointer and shrink it from the left when needed. 
If the target sum is found, print the starting and ending indices of the subarray. If no such subarray exists, display an appropriate message.

📌 CONSTRAINTS:
1 ≤ N ≤ 10⁵  
Array elements are positive integers  
Target is a positive number  
Use sliding window (two pointers) only  
Time complexity must be O(N)

